#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 365 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The PCF8574 is an I2C-based 8-bit GPIO expander. The
object provides 8 additional GPIO pins (0–7) controlled over the I2C
bus \, which is useful when the Raspberry Pi's native GPIO pins are
not enough.;
#X obj 230 88 cnv 1 2 60 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -221520 -1 0;
#X text 240 153 Each pin can be configured independently as input or
output using the [input( and [output( methods. Pins configured as output
can be written with [write( or [write_all( \, pins configured as input
can be read with [read( or [read_all(.;
#X obj 230 158 cnv 1 2 75 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -158925 -1 0;
#X text 240 238 The [impulse( method sends a pulse of the specified
length to a pin configured as output: the pin is set high \, and after
the given time it is automatically set low.;
#X obj 230 243 cnv 1 2 45 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -158925 -1 0;
#X text 240 293 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 318 • Expanding GPIO — adding 8 extra pins to a Raspberry
Pi project \, for example to drive LEDs \, relays or read buttons and
sensors.;
#X text 250 373 • Interrupt-driven input — using the @irq property
to connect the expander's interrupt pin to a Raspberry Pi GPIO \, so
that pin changes are reported without polling.;
